# Trivy exceptions.
#
# Every entry here is a finding we have decided to accept, with a reason and an
# expiry. An exception without an expiry is not an exception, it is a permanent
# blind spot - so each one is dated, and Trivy re-reports it after that date.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go modules compiled into the Caddy binary (target: usr/bin/caddy)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# These are not our dependencies and cannot be patched from here: they are
# statically linked into the upstream Caddy release binary.
#
# Verified rather than assumed. The newest published image (caddy:2-alpine,
# v2.11.4) is built against Go 1.26.3, and every one of these needs 1.26.4 or
# later. `apk --no-cache upgrade` in the Dockerfile fixes the Alpine packages -
# it did, taking the count from 21 to 14 - but cannot touch a compiled binary.
#
# The escape hatch, if these become material: build Caddy from source with
# xcaddy on a newer Go toolchain. That trades a maintained third-party release
# for a build we own, which is a real ongoing cost and not currently justified
# for a proxy that terminates TLS and serves static files.
#
# Exposure is worth stating: Caddy is the only internet-facing container here.
# That argues for reviewing this on a schedule rather than setting and
# forgetting it.
#
# REVIEW BY 2026-11-30 - re-scan and delete any entry upstream has fixed.

